<title>UK: LIFFE May white sugar delivery totals 1,781 lots.</title>
<headline>LIFFE May white sugar delivery totals 1,781 lots.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>A total of 1,781 lots of white sugar, equivalent to 89,050 tonnes, was delivered against the London May No.5 contract after it expired on Tuesday, the London International Financial Futures Exchange (LIFFE) said.</p>
<p>Details are as follows:</p>
<p>SELLER	   LOTS     BUYER			PORT</p>
<p>Bache	     675     Bache		 Immingham</p>
<p>Bache	     483     Sucre Export	Immingham</p>
<p>Bache		 9     Bache		  Flushing</p>
<p>Bache		 7     Sucre Export	 Flushing</p>
<p>E D &amp; F Man     312     Bache		     Gijon</p>
<p>E D &amp; F Man     224     Sucre Export	    Gijon</p>
<p>E D &amp; F Man	12     Bache		   Hamburg</p>
<p>E D &amp; F Man	 8     Sucre Export	  Hamburg</p>
<p>E D &amp; F Man	12     Bache		 Eemshaven</p>
<p>E D &amp; F Man	 9     Sucre Export	Eemshaven</p>
<p>Refco		17     Bache		   Rostock</p>
<p>Refco		13     Sucre Export	  Rostock</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
